      "location": "Definition",
      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "It defines every equation of the form “F(x,u,Du)=0” as “fully nonlinear.” Its direct dependency def-linear-semilinear-quasilinear-and-fully-nonlinear-pde says an order-one equation is fully nonlinear only when its dependence on the highest-order jet is not affine. For example F(x,z,p)=p_1 is affine in p and therefore is not fully nonlinear under that dependency, but it satisfies the stated definition. The definition needs a non-affinity condition on Du, or wording that it is defining a general first-order equation rather than a fully nonlinear one.",
